E010 — Risk-Ranked Coordinator Worklist
Implementation complete: 52 tasks, plus 43 bug tasks from four QC iterations.
42 of the 43 are closed. **T081 is open and cannot be closed on this branch.**

## Not release-ready — one gate is open by design

This feature's own plan declares a release gate it does not meet. `specs/sad.md:124`
sketches the primary flow as `GET /lines?project=…`; `contracts/openapi.yaml`
declares `/worklist` under `/api/v1`. plan.md:46 and HINT-003 both state the
consequence in E010's words: "this feature does not pass QC while the registered
primary flow and this contract name different addresses."

The amendment is not E010's to perform. project-instructions.md:94 — "Amendments
to the documents named in this section are serialized... it is performed on the
default branch... A feature branch records the need for an amendment and does not
perform it." So the gate closes when `specs/sad.md`'s primary flow is amended on
`main`, and E010's QC is re-run after it lands.

`.completed` records that implementation is finished, which it is. `.qc-passed`
must not be written until T081 closes. Iterations 1-3 did not check this
condition; iteration 4 did.

