T076 corrected this marker, and T085 added the supersession note to spec.md's own
Compliance Check, which had been reached by neither re-run.

## What four iterations of QC actually found

43 defects. **Every finding after iteration 1 was an artifact claiming more than
the repository does, rather than a fault in what it does** — with one exception,
T083, a formatting gate that genuinely fails CI. The recurring shape is narrower
than that and worth naming: a bug task filed against N sites is fixed at the one
site its title names. T071 named three task entries and left five in plan.md
(T078); T078's own fix got two of the five replacements wrong (T089) and split a
heading (T088); T072 named two sites and closed one (T084); T073 fixed the weight
half of an assertion and left the size half (T079). Four iterations, same shape.

  Iteration 1 (T053-T065) — 13 findings, mostly in code
    T053  Principle VII — the security limitation record stated two falsehoods
          and its reversal trigger had fired.
    T054  FR-042 — the scoping control was absent in the empty-filter state.
    T055  FR-029 — the row-level stale mark was unimplemented.
    T056  FR-051 — bounded forms were not announced as words.
    T057  The E2E seed truncated the shared development database.
    T058-T065  Test-coverage, provenance and accuracy gaps.

  Iteration 2 (T066-T075) — 10 findings, six of them iteration 1's own claims
    T066  T055's fix added a per-row `as_of_is_stale` field and widened the
          contract to admit it. FR-029 says the mark "needs no new figure and no
          new field" and FR-027 closes the secondary region at three items. The
          field is gone; the interface composes the mark from
          `meta.forecast_run.stale`, and the contract is back to three.
    T067  T060's three properties read through a helper defined in the test file
          rather than through `rows.miss_probability`, and one asserted `x == x`.
          They now drive production code: mutating the survival read with a
          complement, or with an off-by-one, fails them.
    T068  tasks.md claimed a `test:` commit precedes each `feat:` commit. It does
          not, and the sentence is corrected rather than back-filled.
    T069  The invocation-record test issued no adjustment-carrying request.
    T070  plan.md recorded a Playwright request-recording observation that does
          not exist.
    T071  Three task entries named files that were never created.
    T072  plan.md recorded the benchmark population as "~200 open lines"; it is 16.
    T073  The type-scale assertion measured the secondary container rather than
          its descendants.
    T074  The compliance re-audit against v1.2.7.
    T075  `src/api` did not pin `--basetemp`. Pinned, and measured by
          `tests/test_scratch_location.py` rather than declared.

  Iteration 3 (T076-T080) — 5 findings, all this marker or the plan overstating
    T076  This marker named v1.2.7 after the re-audit at v1.2.8.
    T077  Root-check figure read 249; measured 292. Import-contract count read 3
          with no scope named; the repository keeps 11 across three entries.
    T078  T071's correction reached three task entries and left the same two
          names at five points in plan.md and once in tasks.md's Dependencies.
    T079  T073's correction reached the font-weight half and left the font-size
          half measuring the container. Now measured over descendants and
          mutation-checked: a descendant at 2rem fails it at 32 px against a
          16 px primary while the container stays at 14 px — which is exactly
          why the original passed.
    T080  This marker listed mypy among the checks E010 passes. No mypy runs
          over E010's code.

  Iteration 4 (T081-T095) — 15 findings; 14 closed, T081 open by design
    T081  **OPEN, BLOCKED.** The release gate above. Recorded, not performed.
    T082  This marker reported three entries as not pinning `--basetemp` one
          commit after plan.md had been corrected to say they do. All four pin it.
    T083  `ruff format --check` failed at the root on an E010-owned file, so the
          CI format gate failed as the branch stood, while this marker reported
          ruff clean over all four tiers. The only iteration-4 finding that was
          a fault rather than a claim.
    T084  T072 named two sites and closed one; plan.md:117 still read
          "~200 lines" against plan.md:186's corrected 16.
    T085  spec.md's Compliance Check still recorded v1.2.4 with no supersession
          note, reached by neither re-audit.
    T086  The web coverage scope was stated as src/web; it is src/web/app/worklist.
    T087  T078 fixed the filenames in T040 and T045 and left the `WTS/` directory
          token, so both corrected names resolved to a directory that does not
          hold them.
    T088  T078's edit anchored on a substring and split a section heading.
    T089  Two of T078's five replacement paths were themselves wrong.
    T090  The Instructions Check misstated where this feature's web tests live.
    T091  manual-test.md said 18 specs (19), cited T053 for T057's fix, and its
          cleanup step deleted E005's dataset from a database the seed has not
          touched since T057.
    T092  CHK006's evaluator note was a third live site of the corrected
          benchmark population.
    T093  The benchmark-population narrowing lacked Principle VII's reversal
          trigger and production-scale alternative.
    T094  This marker claimed `.prettierignore` excludes the coverage directory.
          It does not; `.gitignore` does, which Prettier reads by default.
    T095  qc-report.md held no record of iteration 3.

## Reported, outside E010's scope

  SC-017 and SC-018 are measured against the frozen fixture's 16 lines rather
  than the ~200-line working population the spec's Assumptions state. Recorded
  in plan.md:186 in Principle VII's four-part form (T093), with the reversal
  trigger being the first run against a realistic population or the first
  coexistence of the two datasets.

  pip-audit has produced no result on either side: it cannot run locally (TLS
  interception) and its CI step has not executed yet. Recorded as unmeasured
  rather than as a null result.

  The security limitation's reversal trigger has fired for /src/web — 3 high
  advisories on production dependencies (next, postcss, sharp). Upgrading `next`
  across a major is E001 scaffold work with its own verification surface.

  eslint reports 2 warnings, 0 errors, neither in a file E010 owns: an unused
  `readFileSync` in `src/web/__tests__/boundary.test.ts` (E001's file, which E010
  has never modified), and an unused directive inside the generated
  `src/web/coverage/` output. That directory is skipped by Prettier and git via
  `src/web/.gitignore:14`, which Prettier reads by default, but
  `eslint.config.mjs`'s `globalIgnores` does not list it — so it is linted
  whenever a coverage run precedes a lint run. Both are E001 toolchain
  configuration.

  On a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true`, `npx prettier --check .`
  reports files in src/web as unformatted that are clean as stored in git
  (`git show HEAD:<path> | npx prettier --check --stdin-filepath <path>` passes).
  The difference is CRLF in the working tree against the LF that is committed, so
  the CI gate on Linux is unaffected. Recorded so the next reader does not chase it.
